# Recoder — Open Work (not-done only)

Backlog of outstanding work only. Shipped history lives in git + commit messages + closed `bd` issues.
Source-of-truth order: plan.md (execution) → remaining.md (paid-user gate) → prd.md/product.md (product) → this file.

## Paid-user launch gate (blocks first paid users)

Each item below is the *remaining* slice; the supporting implementation has shipped and is covered by local tests.

- **GitHub delivery** — deployed GitHub adapter/webhook verification against the production PR-artifact flow. (Shipped: typed repo connection, task↔branch delivery links, PR/preview artifacts, check/review sync, issue linking, signed-payload webhook ingestion + local regression.)
- **Task timeline** — deployed UI/API verification of the shared `task → A2A ingress → runtime events → artifact → PR → preview → approval` timeline against real paid-user data (not demo/per-page state). (Shipped: shared run history, gateway→Agent OS projection, `/api/agent-os/events` legal state changes, RunHistoryService regression.)
- **CloudEvent outbox** — production enablement + NATS JetStream verification on the deployed stack. (Shipped: `GET /api/agent-os/outbox`, durable `recoder.>` drain, opt-in drain loop via `AGENT_OS_OUTBOX_DRAIN_ENABLED` / `_INTERVAL_MS`.)
- **Instruction provenance** — deployed UI verification of compiled InstructionBundle artifacts. (Shipped: compile/ingest → `instruction_bundle` artifact storage with source/memory/approval/provenance + content hash, summary + Agents control-plane rows.)
- **Runtime evidence** — deployed runtime-adapter coverage/proof for real sandbox sessions across every paid-user runtime. (Shipped: runtime-evidence model + `/api/agent-os/runtime-evidence`, A2A terminal-result persistence into evidence + outbox.)
- **MCP approval loop** — deployed PM verification against real MCP tool calls. (Shipped: canonical `PolicyDecision` records, `needs_approval` vs hard deny, PM approve/reject wired to `/api/agent-os/approvals/:id/{approve,reject}`.)
- **Live edge/preview rollout** — DNS, TLS, protected preview hosts, rate limits, WAF hooks, production verification (`recoder-zvss`). *Infra access required.*
- **Hetzner deploy hygiene** — resolve local↔prod git divergence so full deploys don't need scoped checkout/build handling (`recoder-js56`). *Infra access required.*
- **Production traffic/abuse controls** — real-traffic threshold tuning + production alert review (`recoder-a9rp`, `recoder-rbc2`). (Shipped: rate-limit→abuse escalation/blocklist, opt-in payload inspection via `ABUSE_PAYLOAD_INSPECTION_ENABLED`.)

## Security / hardening

- **[recoder-0zso] `/api/a2a/*` auth — remaining surface closure.** Done: admin auth fails closed when `RECODER_A2A_ADMIN_TOKEN` is unset; bridge tokens are session/secret-verified (no anon bypass); 29/35 routes use `authenticateRequest` with the REST/git/terminal/workspace/search/scratchpad/connector/orchestration/workflow slices closed and owner-scoped workspace access. **Still open:** broad per-route enforcement on the legacy `/api/a2a/*` task + workspace *mutating* routes that internal services (agency/agents/pm) currently call **without** auth headers — requires an internal-service-key auth path + full product-loop runtime verification before enforcing (must not break server-to-server calls). `.well-known/agent.json` stays public by spec.

## Capability layer — follow-ups (prod, infra access required)

- Self-host on prod: bring up Qdrant + ziti (NOT Ollama/vLLM — 16GB/no-GPU box); set cloud LLM + Gemini keys per `docker-backend/.env.capabilities.recoder-server`.
- Stand up OpenZiti controller end-to-end + provision a runner (`scripts/provision-ziti-runner.sh`); needs CA trust (`NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`).
- Free prod disk (94% used; 135GB is vcpeer — do not touch) before enabling capability backends.

